  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The distance between two subway stations is $1\\,km.$ How much is this distance in meters?",
  "worked_solution": "A table showing the metric units of length is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilometer | $\\text{km}$ | $1\\,\\text{km}=1\\,000\\,\\text{m}$ |\n| Meter | $\\text{m}$ | Base Unit |\n| Centimeter | $\\text{cm}$ | $100\\,\\text{cm}=1\\,\\text{m}$ |\n| Millimeter | $\\text{mm}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\text{mm}=1\\,\\text{m}$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\text{km}$ is equivalent to $1\\,000\\,\\text{m}.$",
